WEBVTT

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:06.940
Hey, look.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.060
The first-years have already scattered.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.190
Someone must've raised the pace 
and broken the group apart.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.310
Probably.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.920
And a fake attack couldn't 
have scattered them this much.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:25.420
It's someone who can maintain a high 
average speed over a long period of time.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.040
It must be the experienced first-years...

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.590
Kaburagi and Danchiku.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.720
<i>K-Kaburagi-kun...</i>

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.720
Sorry, Onoda-senpai!

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.420
Forgive me for being rude on 
the first day of the school!

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.600
It's fine! I'm not worried about it.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.980
You forgive me?

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.370
You should make him obligated to you.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:54.220
Uh, if you're so worried about it,
why don't you show me

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.570
with your riding at the 
upcoming first-year race?

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:58.830
I'll show you...

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.770
...exactly how I ride!

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.640
Kaburagi and Danchiku are riding alone!

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:11.190
No, someone's going after them! Who is it?

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.560
That jersey...

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.630
We still can't see the front.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.860
They're riding pretty fast.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.980
We've passed most of the first-years.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:31.000
Have Kaburagi-kun and Danchiku-kun 
already won the first-year race?

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.970
We have passed most of the first-years, but...

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:38.310
we haven't passed any second-years yet.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:40.800
I see the front!

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.260
It's Kaburagi and Danchiku!

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.410
And there's one more guy!

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.000
Sugimoto-kun!

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.440
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:24.050
<i>RIDE.10 The Sugimoto Brothers' Bond</i>

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.050
Five Inter-High jerseys 
are already accounted for.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:31.350
Who wears the remaining one will 
be determined in this first-year race.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.690
Sugimoto-kun is amazing.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.340
Not bad, Sugimoto.

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.610
<i>Quit trembling!</i>

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.560
<i>I'll become the sixth man.</i>

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.370
<i>I'll be in the Inter-High.</i>

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.660
<i>I'll wear this jersey.</i>

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.550
He's sticking right to them.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.370
Sugimoto-kun's dancing with intensity.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.720
Sugimoto's still keeping up.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.040
He's not dropping his pace.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.140
Amazing.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.270
Hey, hotshot, don't you have anything to say?

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:01.820
That's our Sugimoto.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:02.600
Not really.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:03.200
What?

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.260
He still has a lot to learn.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.280
Talk about unpleasant.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.280
Go on being a hotshot forever, hotshot.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:14.940
He hasn't shown his true strength yet.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.510
What's going on? He's breaking 
away from the group.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:19.230
Aw, no.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.440
Is he out of strength? He's wobbling.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:24.950
What on earth is he doing?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.080
No way! He passed Kaburagi and Danchiku!

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.920
And he's pulling ahead of them!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:40.000
He's trying to break away!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.380
Amazing.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.170
<i>Sugimoto...</i>

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.170
He's accelerating! Seriously?

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.430
I heard you're going to ride 
in the first-year race.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:50.560
Yeah. Thanks for all your help, Imaizumi.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:56.270
I don't have time to worry about 
being a second-year or my pride.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:01.370
I know it's an unreasonable request, but I...

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.180
Actually, the rest is just 
my delusion, so forget it.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.310
I'll do my best.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.920
I see. Good luck.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.840
Yeah. Watch me from the van.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.790
<i>I'll show you.</i>

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:23.260
<i>I'd seen Imaizumi in several
races in Chiba before.</i>

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.570
<i>He was tall, cool, and 
the center of attention.</i>

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.610
<i>I thought he and I had nothing in common.</i>

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.230
<i>But we got into the same high 
school and joined the same club.</i>

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:39.070
<i>Imaizumi, if I'm able to become the 
sixth man and ride in the Inter-High,</i>

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:43.130
<i>I want to ride as hard as I can.</i>

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.630
<i>I'll ride with all my might for 
the team, and in the end—</i>

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:49.710
<i>Actually, this might be delusional.</i>

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.330
We're counting on you, Imaizumi!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.230
I know, Teru!

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:01.580
<i>I hope I can push your back 
just before the finish line.</i>

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.760
<i>Imaizumi...</i>

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:06.670
He's pulling ahead again!

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.780
Not bad, Sugimoto!

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:13.280
But the guys behind him seem like 
they have a lot of strength left.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:17.150
You're exactly right, Onoda.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:19.350
It's not that they can't go after him.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.110
They're choosing not to.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.830
Why would they do that?

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.410
They still have half the course left,

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:28.230
and the second half includes 
the brutal Minegayama.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.040
If he's weak, then letting him get 
away won't have any consequences.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.170
He'll quickly exhaust himself 
and come falling back.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:35.580
Needlessly exerting themselves 
would be a waste.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.680
They have the advantage 
of ability and numbers.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:41.600
If it comes down to it, they can 
make up a few minutes' difference.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.010
That's what they're thinking.

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.280
They're treating him like 
a bird inside a birdcage.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.860
No matter how much it flaps 
its wings, it can't fly.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:52.510
But that can lead to a sudden comeback

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.760
when they miscalculate that bird's strength.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.520
Sugimoto is a weak sprinter.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.900
They must've thought the same thing.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.020
But his legs are built for long rides.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.490
He can maintain a high average 
speed over a long period of time.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:15.030
Sugimoto's probably gone much farther 
ahead than they're imagining.

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:17.370
<i>The dam! I made it to the dam.</i>

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:21.120
<b>Kameishi Dam
Parking Lot</b>

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.120
<i>Now I just have to circle around 
it and climb up Minegayama.</i>

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.340
<i>I'm doing well.</i>

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:22.960
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.510
This isn't good. This doesn't feel right.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:33.760
Danchiku, I judged him to be beneath our 
concern with the weak way he passed us.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.390
But his legs might be...

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:40.270
There's no way they won't notice.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.750
Have you loosened up yet, Danchiku?

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:48.220
Yeah. That was enough to relax me.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:51.030
<i>Danchiku's shackles are off.</i>

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:56.050
Let's ride all out to catch him, Issa!

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.740
Yeah, Danchiku!

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.750
Go!

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.400
They're fast!

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.250
They made it to the dam in no time!

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.010
We still haven't caught up yet, Danchiku.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.880
He's way faster than we thought.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.000
<i>But we're even faster.</i>

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.050
<i>When Danchiku's freed from 
the shackles of anxiety,</i>

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:20.020
<i>he rides so quickly, I'd fall 
behind if I wasn't careful.</i>

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.560
Roar, Danchiku!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:26.400
The SS logo on their chests...

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:30.940
Team SS the one of the strongest 
major teams in Chiba,

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.620
composed of riders ranging from 
middle school students to adults.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:35.530
It has a fifteen-member roster,

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.610
and every month they
race to compete for slots.

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:40.790
And they've remained on the team.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.750
<i>As middle school students?</i>

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.670
The "SS" in their name
stands for "Speed Shot."

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.380
They take down their prey at top speed.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.710
Hey, you had me scared for a moment.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:55.820
If we'd been just a few minutes slower...

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.260
You might've gotten us.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.960
They passed Sugimoto in a second!

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.890
He managed to get ahead of them, too.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.380
<i>Sugimoto...</i>

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.280
After them, Sugimoto!

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.370
Go after their butts!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.710
If you don't chase now, you'll 
fall behind completely!

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.080
Your defeat will be certain!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.920
Is it hard? Don't think you can do it?

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.920
Whenever you feel that way, just remember...

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.250
It's hard for you, but it's 
just as hard for them!

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:34.630
Whoever manages to hold on wins!

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.580
<i>Don't let go, don't let go!</i>

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.260
<i>I'm going to be the sixth man.</i>

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.710
<i>Thank you, Imaizumi.</i>

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:44.090
He got a second wind!

00:09:44.090 --> 00:09:46.370
Sugimoto-kun's accelerating again!

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:52.080
What, hotshot? You're not putting on airs?

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.690
That was amazing. You were 
so passionate just now.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:55.840
Don't mock me.

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:59.770
I was just telling him 
it's time to go for it.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.240
<i>Telling him how he felt?</i>

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:07.620
<i>These guys are carrying on the spirit 
of Sohoku High School, Kinjou.</i>

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:12.620
I'm not trying to provide 
Sugimoto any extra support.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:16.480
If he wins, it'll be because he caught up.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:20.760
He's desperately trying to catch up now, 
but there's no telling if he will.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.510
<i>Be strong, be strong.</i>

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.390
<i>I have to chase after them now.</i>

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:31.320
<i>If I don't catch up, I don't stand a chance.</i>

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:33.900
<i>I'm riding so I can claim 
one of those jerseys.</i>

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.400
<i>There's two of them.</i>

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.650
No, don't think about it.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.400
Just catch up. Catch up.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.780
<i>I can do it.</i>

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.540
<i>Be strong, be strong.</i>

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.750
<i>Everyone's watching from behind.</i>

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.210
<i>Once I make it over this hill, I'll see them.</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.060
<i>I don't see them. They're fast.</i>

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:56.920
<i>My legs aren't strong enough to catch them.</i>

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:59.540
<i>I told you not to think!</i>

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:00.340
<i>I'll catch up.</i>

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.710
<i>It's hard for them, too. It must be.</i>

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:05.760
<i>This race is my last chance.</i>

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:09.630
What should we do, Teshima?

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.400
Go after the leaders.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:17.130
Realistically, Sugimoto won't 
catch up to Kaburagi and Danchiku.

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:21.490
They should already be beginning the 
final climb up Minegayama.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.490
<b>Minegayama</b>

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.490
<b>Kameishi Dam
 Entrance</b>

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.440
But Sugimoto-kun is—

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.000
We have to watch the leaders ride.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:30.710
This race will determine the final 
member of the Inter-High team.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.580
Got it.

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:36.130
Wait, what?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.090
<i>Huh? Guys?</i>

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.340
Wait.

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:50.900
Wait. This is the last...

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:55.020
Wait, Imaizumi!

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.400
Sugimoto-kun stopped pedaling.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.560
Can't we turn the car around and—

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:03.240
Onoda, this is a race.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:08.330
Knowing this could happen, 
Sugimoto chose to participate.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:09.700
Imaizumi-kun...

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.990
I thought he could do more.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:25.230
<i>Kinjou-san said Sohoku High School 
riders support each other.</i>

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.020
<i>I thought he could do better.</i>

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:34.050
<i>That he had the ability to do better 
if he had teammates to help him.</i>

00:12:34.050 --> 00:12:37.860
<i>If he had teammates supporting him,
then this race...</i>

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.240
All right.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.910
I finally caught up.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.410
You really are fast, Brother.

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:51.810
Sadatoki...

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:56.080
<b>Minegayama</b>

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:58.080
No one's pursuing us.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.000
Once we reach the top of this mountain,

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.490
it's all downhill to the 
finish line, Danchiku.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.260
This race is ours.

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.180
We're going to the Inter-High, Danchiku.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.390
Don't celebrate so much, Issa.
You're like a child.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.960
When would I celebrate, if not now?

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.480
I am a child, Danchiku.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.960
One who's been presented 
with all the toys he wanted

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.820
and told to play with them 
to his heart's content.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.190
I am a child!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:26.730
I'm excited.

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:28.720
I'm getting chills, Danchiku.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:31.200
I finally get to go.

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.860
The race I saw when I tagged along 
on my father's business trip

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:35.580
was my first Inter-High.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:37.880
I was dumbfounded.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:39.500
I was so excited, I leaped into the air.

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:43.710
It blew away my concepts
of "fast" and "strong."

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.280
It was an awesome race.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.640
I decided then that I would 
participate in that race.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:52.980
Not that I could, but that I would.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.910
I'd get stronger and participate.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:14:00.820
There are plenty of strong riders 
in the world, but that's fine.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.580
I've become super strong.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:04.320
I'll battle them and win.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:08.820
Conquering the Inter-High is my goal!

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.830
Let's do it. We can do it, Danchiku.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.200
After all, I have you with me.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.660
Stop. You're embarrassing me.

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:19.970
Huh?

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:21.560
They're falling back.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:22.620
Teshima-san!

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:23.460
What is it?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:26.800
You haven't forgotten our promise, have you?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:30.030
If Danchiku and I finish first 
and second in this race,

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.300
you'll let both of us 
onto the Inter-High team.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.080
Yeah.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.220
All right!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:38.130
I, Kaburagi Issa, along with Danchiku, 
will ride in the Inter-High!

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:40.240
Hey, what kind of promise is that?

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:44.220
B-Both of them? Does that mean someone 
from the current lineup is out?

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.840
It's a world dictated by ability. It happens.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:49.480
Um, who is it? Who is it?

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:52.080
It's me, isn't it?

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:54.160
Good luck, everyone.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.510
He's so mentally weak.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.540
Onoda-san, it's on.

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:00.540
I went to see the Inter-High last year.

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:02.920
The finish line was at Mt. Fuji.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.590
Honestly, it was a mesmerizing race.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.800
Indescribably so.

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:10.490
My entire body went numb.

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:13.900
I became depressed on the way home 
and couldn't sleep for three days.

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:19.820
I was frustrated from the bottom of 
my heart that I wasn't on that stage.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:24.830
Because I was shown that you 
were far stronger than me.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:27.110
That's why...

00:15:29.390 --> 00:15:33.820
I'll surpass you at this summer's Inter-High.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.620
I'll surpass you!

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.630
What's your goal for this year's Inter-High?

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:43.110
A second consecutive general 
classification victory?

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.590
I don't have to win.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:50.920
I want to be with Imaizumi-kun
 and Naruko-kun,

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.880
Teshima-san and Aoyagi-san,

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.950
riding together as hard we can.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.640
I want to give everything I have 
against Manami-kun and Midousuji-kun.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:04.900
And in the end, I hope someone on our team
 has the chance to finish first.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:10.510
Also, this is just me being greedy, but 
I'd like to report to the upperclassmen...

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.450
<i>To Makishima-san...</i>

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:16.120
That we did it.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.590
Report?

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:23.540
You are greedy. You couldn't be greedier.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:28.500
We'll have to practice super hard, Onoda-kun.

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:30.460
Yeah.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.910
<i>What kind of solidarity is this?</i>

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:34.220
Kaburagi!

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:40.920
Last year we reeled in a thin thread that 
was about to break and won together.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:44.640
It may seem unrefined, but that's 
how Sohoku High School races.

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:46.290
Sound lame?

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:50.270
Kaburagi, you already think 
you've won, even though

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.240
you haven't broken the finish line's tape.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.110
What?

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:58.470
Sugimoto, the man you passed and 
left behind, may be unreliable,

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:00.870
but he possesses the spirit 
of Sohoku High School.

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:07.290
If he hasn't given up on winning 
this race, then he'll come.

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:10.050
He'll catch up to you.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.620
Is that a threat?

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.440
That's impossible.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:17.030
In other words, you want me 
to stop talking and ride.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.800
I understand. Sorry!

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.190
Let's head to the finish line, Danchiku!

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:22.060
Yeah!

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:24.020
A threat?

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:25.980
No.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:34.740
I've just seen miracles like
that happen plenty of times.

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:35.810
<i>Sugimoto.</i>

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:36.490
Is it Sugimoto?

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.490
Sadatoki-kun!

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:40.830
Not yet. I won't give up yet.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.540
I see them, Brother! It's the van.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:45.370
I can't believe the brothers 
caught up together.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.520
This is unexpected.

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.710
Sugimoto-kun caught up!

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.710
<i>I'll become the sixth man.</i>

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.800
Their synchronization is unbelievable.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:59.270
Amazing. Sugimoto-kun hasn't given up yet.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:01.720
But there's two more kilometers to the peak.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.310
Once they're past that, it's downhill.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.670
Sugimoto's legs aren't 
enough to close the gap.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:09.560
How much they can catch up to Kaburagi 
and Danchiku on this climb will be key.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.520
<i>Sugimoto... and his brother.</i>

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.820
<i>The brothers' synchronization...</i>

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:20.450
<i>When he came to practice before,
their synchronization was inefficient.</i>

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:25.140
<i>But now both of them have got it down.</i>

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.040
<i>They must've practiced 
together for this moment.</i>

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.040
<i>No.</i>

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:31.080
<i>Sugimoto's will raised them up.</i>

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.550
<i>It's this situation that gave rise to it.</i>

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.670
I'll become the sixth man.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:38.930
Go! Go, Sadatoki!

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:40.800
Yeah, Brother!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:47.830
Brother, we'll catch up to 
Aburagi-kun and Danchiku-kun.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.850
I'm counting on you, Sadatoki. 
But it's Kaburagi.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:53.610
<i>Thank you, Sadatoki.</i>

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:59.990
<i>If you hadn't caught up to me then, 
I would've given up on this race.</i>

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:04.910
Sadatoki, how? Did you 
make it here on your own?

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:05.450
Yeah.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.120
I wanted to ride with you, Brother.

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:14.270
<i>In that moment, I felt as though one strand 
of the broken string inside my heart</i>

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:15.840
<i>was still connected.</i>

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:19.300
Sadatoki, can you keep riding?

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:23.720
Kaburagi and Danchiku just passed me.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:26.550
I want to catch up and pass them again.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:29.360
Will you help me, Sadatoki?

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:32.810
I want to go to the Inter-High 
as the sixth man.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.980
That was the first time. The first!

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:36.570
What?

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:40.560
You're cool and strong and know everything.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:42.820
You've always pulled me forward.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:47.830
But that's the first time 
you've asked me for something.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:52.250
So, I'll do it. I promise I'll take you there.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.540
<i>Sadatoki!</i>

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:57.250
Also, um...

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.450
You really do look cool in that jersey.

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:03.200
It looks great on you, Brother!

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:07.560
<i>When you were little, 
you were such a crybaby.</i>

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:13.570
<i>You followed me around saying,
"I can't," and, "I'm not confident."</i>

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:18.280
<i>It's okay. It's okay now, Sadatoki.</i>

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:19.860
<i>You can do anything.</i>

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:22.110
<i>Your brother can attest to that.</i>

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:25.890
Follow me. You can do it, Sadatoki.

00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:29.180
We'll cross the finish line together.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:31.620
Yeah!

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:36.170
<i>Even though Imaizumi tried to cheer 
me up, my legs stopped moving once.</i>

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:39.450
<i>But Sadatoki saved me.</i>

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:43.380
<i>For Sadatoki's sake, if it's still possible,</i>

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:48.760
<i>I want to do my best to reel in 
this last thread one more time.</i>

00:20:49.590 --> 00:20:50.720
<i>One more time!</i>

00:20:54.850 --> 00:21:00.700
Sugimoto caught up to Kaburagi and 
Danchiku just 50 meters before the peak!

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.520
Sugimoto's amazing!

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:04.740
Sadatoki-kun and Sugimoto-kun 
are both amazing!

00:21:06.230 --> 00:21:08.890
Was this unexpected, too, Teshima?

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:12.790
Road races certainly are 
fantastic, aren't they?

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.630
Damn it! I underestimated them.

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:19.890
Who's that big guy?

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:21.890
Let's head to the finish line, Sadatoki!

00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:23.080
Yeah, Brother!

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:24.920
Pedal harder! Faster, Danchiku!

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:28.520
They're neck and neck at the peak!

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:30.980
Now it's downhill to the finish line!

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:06.660
I've been thinking, since we're the 
new generation of Sohoku High School,

00:23:06.660 --> 00:23:09.020
why don't we change our jersey's color?

00:23:09.020 --> 00:23:10.860
A flashy red would be cool.

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:13.910
You have terrible taste. Blue is better.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:16.200
Then we'd be the same as 
Hakone Academy High School.

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:17.800
Onoda-kun, what do you think?

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:22.170
Well, red is flashy, but blue is cool.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:27.140
But I like yellow because it's 
a modest but noble color.

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:31.500
I guess you could say it's 
simultaneously cool and cute.

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:32.840
What do you guys think?

00:23:33.270 --> 00:23:35.800
Yellow's good.

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:39.850
<i>NEXT RIDE  Conclusion</i>

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:44.860
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
